<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[
The method `GameWorld.camera()` simply returns the field `this.camera`:

```java
public ICamera camera() {
  return this.camera;
}
```

So `Game.world().camera()` will be `null` exactly when `GameWorld.camera` is `null`.

From the provided code, `camera` is assigned only via `setCamera`:

```java
public void setCamera(final ICamera cam) {
  if (this.camera() != null) {
    Game.loop().detach(camera);
  }

  camera = cam;

  if (cam != null && !Game.isInNoGUIMode()) {
    Game.loop().attach(cam);
    cam.updateFocus();
  }
}
```

Relevant places where `setCamera` is called:

1. **During initialization**:
   ```java
   public static synchronized void init(String... args) {
     ...
     world.setCamera(new Camera());
     ...
   }
   ```
